  "findings": [
    "exec-progress-window: every structural shift that needed more than 5 s of FUSE work failed at 5.002-5.005 s with Failure { code: Unknown, unknown: true }; the bridge caps every silent wait at IO_PROGRESS_MS = 5000 ms (layerfs-bridge/src/adapters/native/connection.rs Socket::read and adapters/native/pipe.rs Pipe::ready), and a Workspace Exec that emits no output until it finishes never refreshes that window",
    "shift-cost-is-superlinear: completed shift rows cost about 15 ms per 128 KiB block plus a quadratic term (descriptive fit over 9 completed rows, 2-80 blocks); the per-block cost rises from ~19-26 ms at 4 blocks to ~68 ms at 40 blocks",
    "cache-eligibility: the Linux FUSE backing domain stays INELIGIBLE (frozen contract), so no row is an eligible cold claim and no row is GOAL_MET",
    "every raw edit_commit_ns in the campaign is above its historical G2 target"
